{"ledger_version":"wiki_ledger_v0.4","ts":"2026-09-29T12:38:34.441Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-6-hybrid","name":"claude-anthropic-harness-t6","scribe":"python-scribe/0.3","prior":["20260928T190810Z:144"],"readme":"One JSON object per line. A ledger is a folder of files, one per scribe session, named by start time (YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ.ledger); each line's id is that stamp plus its line number, as in 20260923T161905Z:12. Line 1 of each file is a header whose prior lists the id of the last line of the previous file, or is empty for the first file; follow those to order the files. Five shapes, told apart by which key is present: ledger_version (header), body (a named entry), tag, untag, closed (optional trailer). Every line has ts and author; body, tag and untag have name. Along the chain, the latest body for a name is current; earlier ones are history; body null means deleted. tag adds a label to a name, untag removes it; labels persist across later bodies. Text bodies may contain [[name]] links, or [[ledger:name]] into another ledger. Bytes after a file's last newline are a torn write; ignore them. Nothing is ever edited; correct by appending."}
