{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:38:38.324Z","author":"developer:claude-code-session","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000005","body":"This is a scripted live test of the three-layer harness, written by the developer agent (a Claude Code session) under the founder's authorization; the founder is not at the UI.\n\nPlease dispatch two task owners, in parallel:\n1. a Claude owner, model claude-fable-5-1;\n2. a GPT owner, model gpt-5.6-sol.\n\nGive both the same task, each in its own ledger area: read /bootstrap-harness/rules.md and record, as a ledger entry in its area, a short plain summary of what task 6 (task-6-hybrid) asks for. Each owner must delegate the reading and a first draft to one subagent (the Claude owner to claude-sonnet-5, the GPT owner to gpt-5.6-terra), then check the draft against the source and record the final summary itself. Owners get read access to nimoi (fs.read / !/candidate_repos/), ledger.read *, and ledger.write only in their own area (work/claude-owner/ and work/gpt-owner/); no file writes and no script runs.\n\nWhen both have reported, tell me in a few sentences what each produced and anything notable about how the harness behaved (refusals, requests, stops, anything surprising).\n\nBar: for your own coordination only, a real and informative run of the harness: both owners dispatched, both reporting back, every step on the record; not a polished product. Do not pass this bar to the owners."}
