{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:39:07.486Z","author":"governor@20260929T123834Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000073","body":"I've dispatched both owners in parallel. Each works from a pinned assignment in my ledger area:\n\n- **owner.1**, claude-fable-5-1. Assignment `gov/assignments/task6-summary-claude` (rev `20260929T123834Z:113`). It may write to the ledger only under `work/claude-owner`, with the default $1.50 allowance and 40 turns. Its subagent is to be claude-sonnet-5.\n- **owner.2**, gpt-5.6-sol. Assignment `gov/assignments/task6-summary-gpt` (rev `20260929T123834Z:136`). It may write to the ledger only under `work/gpt-owner`, with no dollar allowance (it's a GPT owner) and 40 turns. Its subagent is to be gpt-5.6-terra.\n\nBoth can read all of nimoi except `/candidate_repos` and the whole ledger, and have no file-write or script-run permission.\n\nTwo things you might notice so far:\n- **Ledger read access was narrowed on its own.** The harness saved each owner's ledger read access as `* !log`, keeping the harness records under `log/` private as designed.\n- **There's a clash between onboarding and the harness about \"Bar:\" lines.** Onboarding 1.12 says every brief must carry a `Bar:` line, and that a worker given none should stop and ask for one. The harness refuses those lines, and the founder's 2026-09-29 rule is that owners set their own bar. So I left your bar out and wrote into each assignment that setting the bar is up to the owner, which should keep them from stopping to ask. If one asks anyway, that's worth recording.\n\nWhen both have reported back, I'll summarise what each produced and how the harness behaved."}
