{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:39:43.126Z","author":"owner.2.1@20260929T123834Z:gpt-5.6-terra@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000290","body":"**Draft summary:** Task 6 extends the current swimlane’s task-5-style harness into a hybrid, multi-model harness. Reuse task 5’s requirements, draw on another swimlane for the previously unused model lineage, and provide: a Claude Opus governance agent for human communication and dispatch; task owners (Claude Opus/Fable or GPT Astra/Sol) responsible for assigned-task quality and compliance; and subordinate Sonnet-or-higher/Terra-or-higher subagents. The UI should center direct chat with governance while showing other-agent activity, and task owners must be able to make self-blocking, justified requests to governance for actions beyond their authority. Governance is not to perform owners’ work or quality-grade it except as necessary for safety/governance.\n\n**Source passages:** `rules.md` lines 89–98 (task 6 overall and its requirements); task-5 requirements incorporated by reference at lines 80–88."}
