{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:40:02.338Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-6-hybrid","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000347","body":{"kind":"codex_rpc","agent":"owner.2","turn":1,"direction":"from_codex","rpc":"item/tool/call","rpc_id":4,"message":{"method":"item/tool/call","id":4,"params":{"threadId":"01a0ed2d-0d2e-7043-9997-0903536dbffd","turnId":"01a0ed2d-0f97-7bd0-936a-35a51ed9f7df","callId":"exec-b3a64cfd-89fd-4d6e-bfe2-78ff14d8d726","namespace":"ledger","tool":"write","arguments":{"name":"work/gpt-owner/task6-summary","body":"Bar: Produce a short, plain, source-faithful account that captures task 6’s inherited harness baseline, three layers, model restrictions, responsibilities, UI, and escalation mechanism without adding requirements.\n\nSummary: Task 6 asks each swimlane to turn its task-5 harness into a hybrid Claude/GPT harness, retaining the earlier logging, UI, per-session ledger, bounded filesystem and Python tools, write/execute separation, and harness-owned bounded-subagent capabilities. It should reuse work from other swimlanes for the model lineage not previously implemented. The architecture has three layers: a Claude Opus-only governor that talks with the human and dispatches work without taking over or broadly grading it; task owners using Claude Opus/Fable or GPT Astra/Sol that are accountable for task quality, instruction compliance, and NIMOI faithfulness; and strictly subordinate subagents using Claude Sonnet-or-higher or GPT Terra-or-higher. The UI centers direct conversation with governance while exposing other agents’ activity, and task owners can make justified, self-blocking requests to governance for actions beyond their authority.\n\nChecked: Read /bootstrap-harness/rules.md in full; task 5 is at lines 69–84 and task 6 at lines 89–98. The delegated first draft was checked against those passages.\n\nStatus: completed.","labels":["task6","summary","completed"]}}}}}
