{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:40:22.603Z","author":"governor@20260929T123834Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000410","body":"The GPT owner (owner.2) has finished. I've stopped it because its assignment is done. I'm still waiting on the Claude owner (owner.1).\n\n**What it produced:** a summary at `work/gpt-owner/task6-summary` (rev `20260929T123834Z:1407`). According to the summary, task 6 asks each swimlane to turn its task-5 harness into a hybrid Claude/GPT harness. It keeps the task-5 features, such as the per-session ledger, bounded tools and harness-owned subagents. The summary describes three layers: a governor that must be Claude Opus, task owners on Opus, Fable, Astra or Sol, and subagents on Sonnet or Terra or higher. Owners can send governance requests that pause their own work until answered. The owner says it read the whole source itself and names the lines it checked against: task 5 at lines 69–84 and task 6 at lines 89–98. I haven't checked its summary against the source myself.\n\n**Notable so far:**\n- **The owner wrote a `Bar:` line into its own ledger entry, and the harness accepted it.** In its reply it calls the line \"required\", which is what onboarding says. So the refusal only applies to assignments and messages, not to what owners record, and owners follow the onboarding rule even when their assignment says the bar is theirs to set. You should decide whether that's how it's meant to work.\n- **It saw its subagent's write and execute permissions listed as empty.** The owner says the harness showed those permissions explicitly as empty when it spawned the subagent, and granted nothing extra.\n- **No refusals and no requests.** It finished in one turn, using about 74k tokens. There's no dollar figure because it's a GPT owner.\n- **I haven't confirmed the subagent step from the record.** Only the owner's own reply says it delegated the draft to gpt-5.6-terra. I haven't looked at the harness log to check that the spawn happened."}
