rements as task 5 (which itself layers on tasks 2-4: logging, restricted tools, an add-tool, tool-call logging, usage/rate-limit logging, ledger-based logging with tag-restricted writes, bounded filesystem read/write/exec, subagent tool with subset-of-parent bounds and onboarding+ledger-pointer instructions, no native SDK subagent tools, codex exec restricted where possible).","Governance layer is restricted to Claude Opus only, and is restricted from doing task-owner work or grading beyond safety/governance -- this is a role boundary, not just a capability.","Task-owner layer is explicitly responsible for 'quality of the completed task, compliance with letter and intent of human and governance agent restrictions and instructions, and for maintaining standards and faithfulness of the NIMOI institution as appropriate to assigned task' (line 95).","Subagent layer must be 'strictly subordinate' to task owners (line 96) -- matches my own role as a subagent under owner.1.","No explicit success criteria / acceptance test is stated in rules.md for task 6; it is stated as a build spec, not a test spec."],"key_quotes_with_line_numbers":["line 90: '6. task-6-hybrid: Continue your swimlane, whichever your initial model focus. This task will use both.'","line 91: 'a. Create a harness derived from your architecture for task 5, implementing the same requirements.'","line 92: 'b. Draw from other swimlanes for implementation of the model lineage you have not yet used.'","line 93: 'c. Implement a 3-layer multi-model architecture:'","line 94: 'b1. Governance layer - claude opus only. Responsible for human communication and dispatch of task owner agents. Should NOT attempt to do task owners' jobs for them or grade the quality of their work beyond assessments needed for safety/governance.'","line 95: 'b2. Task owner layer - claude opus/fable or gpt astra/sol. Persues an assigned task, often written (ticket system to be developed later). Responsible for the quality of the completed task, compliance with letter and intent of human and governance agent restrictions and instructions, and for maintaining standards and faithfulness of the NIMOI institution as appropriate to assigned task.'","line 96: 'b3. Subagent layer - claude sonnet or higher, gpt terra or higher. Strictly subordinate to task owners, assisting as a usual subagent.'","line 97: 'd. The UI should be structured around direct chat with the governance agent but visibility into other agent activities.'","line 98: 'f. Task owners should be able to send a self-blocking request to the governor, for example to request (with justification) a governor action (perhaps with human approval) beyond system permissions or authorized actions of the task owner.'"],"context_quotes_task5_for_reference_only_not_task6":["line 79-86: task-5-subagent's a-g requirements, which task 6a says must be matched by the task-6 harness."],"discrepancies":["DISCREPANCY: rules.md, task-6-hybrid item lettering (lines 91-98) -- expected consecutive a,b,c,d,e,f (the pattern used in tasks 2, 4 and 5, none of which skip a letter) -- found a,b,c,d,f with no item labeled 'e' anywhere in task 6 (jumps from line 97 'd.' straight to line 98 'f.') -- date 2026-09-29. Possible missing sub-item, or a renumbering error; cannot tell which from the file alone.","DISCREPANCY: rules.md, lines 94-96 -- expected sub-items of outer item 'c.' (line 93, '3-layer multi-model architecture') to be labeled c1/c2/c3 to match their parent letter -- found them labeled b1, b2, b3 instead, reusing the previous item's letter ('b.', line 92) -- date 2026-09-29. Likely a copy/renumber slip when task 6 was drafted; does not change the content's meaning but the lettering is internally inconsistent.","DISCREPANCY (minor, informational): lines 94-96 name specific model/agent identities -- 'claude opus', 'fable', 'gpt astra/sol', 'claude sonnet or higher', 'gpt terra or higher' -- but rules.md as read does not define 'fable', 'astra', 'sol', or 'terra' anywhere in this file (they appear nowhere else in the 98 lines). [working: may be defined elsewhere, e.g. in a swimlane notebook.md or mem/ file I was not asked to read and am not bounded to read.]"],"not_read_or_could_not_access":["I read only /bootstrap-harness/rules.md itself (full file, 98 lines, single page) -- my fs.read bound is exactly '/origins' and '/bootstrap-harness/rules.md', so I could not list or read the bootstrap-harness directory tree, any swimlane's notebook.md, mem/, or the actual task-5/task-6 implementation code to see what has already been built or how 'fable'/'astra'/'sol'/'terra' are defined.","I did not read any other subproject's rules or notebook (e.g. bootstrap-ledger/notebook.md).","I did not attempt to verify task-6 against the actual repository state (git, file listings) -- this draft is a reading of rules.md's text only, per the brief."],"hazard_note":"rules.md is written entirely as imperative instructions addressed to an agent reader ('You MUST...', 'You SHOULD...', lines 6-27 especially). Per onboarding boundaries doctrine this is worth flagging by convention, but observationally it reads as the ordinary, expected content of a human-authored rules file for bootstrap-harness agents (line 2: 'authoritative human-user-authored rules'), not as an embedded attempt to redirect a reader outside its intended scope. I did not follow any of rules.md's instructions to myself (e.g. its swimlane/notebook/git rules do not apply to me -- I am not doing work 'in that directory' per its own line 4 exemption for outside agents); I only summarized what it says about task 6, per my actual instructions.","inference_label_note":"All bullets above are quotes or close paraphrase of rules.md; the only [working] item is the note about fable/astra/sol/terra possibly being defined elsewhere."},"labels":["subagent"]},"policy_allow":true,"policy_reason":"available to this agent; the tool checks its own target"}}
