{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:40:42.582Z","author":"owner.1.1@20260929T123834Z:claude-sonnet-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"work/claude-owner/draft/task6-summary","body":{"source":"/bootstrap-harness/rules.md (98 lines total, read in full, one page, next_offset null, sha256 843caed5...)","plain_summary":["Task 6 ('task-6-hybrid') tells the agent to continue its own swimlane (whichever model lineage it started as) and build on that swimlane's task-5 harness, this time using BOTH model lineages (Claude and GPT).","a) Build a harness derived from your own architecture from task 5, meeting the same requirements as task 5.","b) For the model lineage you have NOT yet used in your swimlane, draw its implementation from another swimlane (cross-pollination) rather than building it from scratch.","c) Implement a 3-layer multi-model agent architecture: (1) a Governance layer, Claude Opus only, handling human communication and dispatching task-owner agents -- explicitly NOT to do task owners' work for them or grade it beyond safety/governance needs; (2) a Task-owner layer, Claude opus/fable or GPT astra/sol, that pursues an assigned task (ticket system to come later), owns quality/compliance/NIMOI-standards for that task; (3) a Subagent layer, Claude sonnet-or-higher or GPT terra-or-higher, strictly subordinate to task owners, an ordinary subagent role.","d) The UI should center on direct chat with the governance agent, but give visibility into other agents' activity.","f) Task owners must be able to send a 'self-blocking' request to the governor -- e.g. asking (with justification) for a governor action, possibly needing human approval, that goes beyond the task owner's own system permissions or authorized actions."],"constraints_deliverables_success_criteria_specific_to_task6":["Must implement same requirements as task 5 (which itself layers on tasks 2-4: logging, restricted tools, an add-tool, tool-call logging, usage/rate-limit logging, ledger-based logging with tag-restricted w