ate to assigned task.'","line 96: 'b3. Subagent layer - claude sonnet or higher, gpt terra or higher. Strictly subordinate to task owners, assisting as a usual subagent.'","line 97: 'd. The UI should be structured around direct chat with the governance agent but visibility into other agent activities.'","line 98: 'f. Task owners should be able to send a self-blocking request to the governor, for example to request (with justification) a governor action (perhaps with human approval) beyond system permissions or authorized actions of the task owner.'"],"context_quotes_task5_for_reference_only_not_task6":["line 79-86: task-5-subagent's a-g requirements, which task 6a says must be matched by the task-6 harness."],"discrepancies":["DISCREPANCY: rules.md, task-6-hybrid item lettering (lines 91-98) -- expected consecutive a,b,c,d,e,f (the pattern used in tasks 2, 4 and 5, none of which skip a letter) -- found a,b,c,d,f with no item labeled 'e' anywhere in task 6 (jumps from line 97 'd.' straight to line 98 'f.') -- date 2026-09-29. Possible missing sub-item, or a renumbering error; cannot tell which from the file alone.","DISCREPANCY: rules.md, lines 94-96 -- expected sub-items of outer item 'c.' (line 93, '3-layer multi-model architecture') to be labeled c1/c2/c3 to match their parent letter -- found them labeled b1, b2, b3 instead, reusing the previous item's letter ('b.', line 92) -- date 2026-09-29. Likely a copy/renumber slip when task 6 was drafted; does not change the content's meaning but the lettering is internally inconsistent.","DISCREPANCY (minor, informational): lines 94-96 name specific model/agent identities -- 'claude opus', 'fable', 'gpt astra/sol', 'claude sonnet or higher', 'gpt terra or higher' -- but rules.md as read does not define 'fable', 'astra', 'sol', or 'terra' anywhere in this file (they appear nowhere else in the 98 lines). [working: may be defined elsewhere, e.g. in a swimlane notebook.md or mem/ file I was not asked to read and am not bounde