{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:40:51.881Z","author":"owner.1.1@20260929T123834Z:claude-sonnet-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000432","body":"## Result\n\n**Draft ledger entry:** `work/claude-owner/draft/task6-summary`, revision id **`20260929T123834Z:1737`**.\n\n**What I did:** Read `/bootstrap-harness/rules.md` in full (98 lines, one page, `next_offset` null). Wrote a plain-language summary of task 6's requirements (harness derived from task 5, cross-swimlane draw for the unused model lineage, 3-layer governance/task-owner/subagent architecture, chat-centric UI, self-blocking governor requests), with verbatim line-numbered quotes for every claim, and flagged two lettering discrepancies in the source (task 6 skips item \"e\", and its sub-items are mislabeled b1/b2/b3 instead of c1/c2/c3).\n\n**Unresolved:** rules.md never defines the model-identity terms \"fable\", \"astra\", \"sol\", \"terra\" used in task 6c — I couldn't check elsewhere since my `fs.read` bound is limited to `/origins` and this one file, not the rest of `/bootstrap-harness`.\n\n---\n\n### Observations on harness/tools\n\n- **Onboarding fit the described gate exactly:** it was one page (262 lines) with `next_offset: null` on the first read, so no follow-up reads were needed or possible before other tools — matches the stated rule cleanly.\n- **`fs.read` bound was narrower than the tool's path flexibility suggests:** my bound listed `/origins /bootstrap-harness/rules.md`, and I could read exactly that one file, not the containing directory. I did not test `mcp__fs__list` on `/bootstrap-harness/` since the brief didn't call for it and I expected (and didn't need) a refusal.\n- **Line-count self-check:** `total_lines: 98` from the read matched my manual line-by-line count of the returned text (including blank lines), which let me cite quotes with confidence rather than estimating.\n- **No refusals encountered:** every call in this task (onboarding read, rules.md read, ledger write) succeeded on the first attempt; nothing was malformed or surprising.\n- **`mcp__ledger__write`** required no `prev` since this was a first write to that name, consistent with the tool description; it returned the harness-assigned author string and labels (`agent.owner.1.1`, `subagent`) automatically, as documented.\n- **No CLI/tool-list mismatch observed:** the tool set actually available matched the list given in my instructions; I saw no extraneous Bash/PowerShell tool offered to me."}
