{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:41:40.625Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-6-hybrid","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000469","body":{"kind":"message","agent":"owner.1","turn":1,"direction":"from_agent","message":{"_type":"AssistantMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolUseBlock","id":"toolu_014uZgVkfCqpN7zE9sF4WD2H","name":"mcp__ledger__write","input":{"name":"work/claude-owner/task6-summary","body":{"title":"What task 6 (task-6-hybrid) asks for: plain summary of /bootstrap-harness/rules.md","Bar":"A short, plain summary a newcomer could act on. Every statement is traceable to a cited line of rules.md (sha256 843caed5bbad0495430bbd194050e4cff0c99688cdaa80504a052287cfec61c2, 98 lines, read in full by owner.1). Nothing the file says about task 6 is left out, and nothing is added. Inferences are labelled [working], and defects in the source are recorded as DISCREPANCY lines, not smoothed over. Not polished prose, and not an interpretation of how to build it.","summary":["Task 6 continues each swimlane's own line of work, whatever model lineage it started with, and 'will use both' (l.90). Rules.md says of swimlanes that for 'hybrid' tasks the lineage and the initial harness architecture 'will be combined' (l.39-40). [working: 'both' = both lineages, Claude and GPT, and so both architectures, Claude Agent SDK and Codex App Server (l.41-42).]","(a) Build a harness derived from your own task-5 harness that meets all of task 5's requirements (l.91). By task 5a (l.80) those include tasks 2-4: message and tool-call logging, restricted code-execution tools, an 'add' tool, usage/rate-limit logging, the local web UI, per-session ledger logging with protected harness entries, and bounded filesystem read. Task 5 adds a bound notation that is concise and the same for parent and child, a tool that writes a ledger entry's body to a workspace, and a tool that runs Python only from a scripts directory, where agents can never both write and execute. It also adds a harness-owned subagent tool (not the SDK's native one) with subset bounds, required onboarding and ledger-pointer instructions, and Codex exec restricted where possible, with any gaps documented (l.81-86).","(b) For the model lineage your swimlane has not used yet, draw the implementation from other swimlanes (l.92). Cross-pollination is permitted (l.46). Other swimlanes may be read but never modified (l.44-45).","(c) Implement a 3-layer multi-model architecture (l.93). Governance layer (l.94): Claude Opus only. It communicates with the human and dispatches task owners. It must not do task owners' jobs or grade their work beyond what safety or governance needs. Task-owner layer (l.95): Claude opus/fable or GPT astra/sol. It pursues an assigned task, often a written one (a ticket system comes later). It is responsible for the task's quality, for complying with the letter and intent of human and governor instructions and restrictions, and for keeping NIMOI's standards and faithfulness as the task requires. Subagent layer (l.96): Claude sonnet or higher, or GPT terra or higher. Strictly subordinate to task owners; an ordinary subagent.","(d) The UI is organised around direct chat with the governance agent, with visibility into what the other agents are doing (l.97).","(f) A task owner can send the governor a self-blocking request, i.e. one it waits on, for example asking with justification for a governor action, perhaps with human approval, beyond its own permissions or authorised actions (l.98).","Rules.md gives no acceptance test or success criteria for task 6. It is a build specification [checked: full read of rules.md l.90-98]. Work in the swimlane also falls under the file's general rules: human-iterative work, pause when unsure, no git, no scope expansion without permission, and a notebook.md and mem/ per swimlane (l.6-27, 49-53)."],"discrepancies":["DISCREPANCY: /bootstrap-harness/rules.md l.90-98. Expected: task 6 items lettered consecutively, as in tasks 2, 4 and 5. Found: a, b, c, d, f with no 'e' (read by owner.1.1 and confirmed by owner.1). The file alone cannot tell a missing item from a lettering slip. 2026-09-29.","DISCREPANCY: /bootstrap-harness/rules.md l.94-96. Expected: the sub-items of item c to be labelled c1-c3. Found: b1, b2, b3. Also, d and f (l.97-98) are indented one space more than a-c. Meaning is unaffected. Read by both agents. 2026-09-29.","DISCREPANCY (minor): /bootstrap-harness/rules.md l.95-96. The file never defines 'fable', 'astra', 'sol' or 'terra', or the order behind 'or higher' (subagent draft). Partly resolved outside the file: this harness's spawn tool lists claude-fable-5-1, gpt-5.6-terra, gpt-5.6-sol and gpt-6-astra as models [checked: mcp__agents__spawn model enum]. The 'or higher' order is still undefined in writing. 2026-09-29."],"provenance":{"draft":"work/claude-owner/draft/task6-summary rev 20260929T123834Z:1737 by owner.1.1 (claude-sonnet-5), briefed by work/claude-owner/tasks/task6-rules-summary-draft rev 20260929T123834Z:644","owner_check":"owner.1 read rules.md in full (same sha256) and checked every quote and line number in the draft. All matched: task 6 is l.90-98, task 5 is l.79-86.","changes_from_draft":["Added l.39-42 (the 'hybrid' tasks combine lineage and architecture), which the draft missed; it bears on what 'use both' means.","Removed an addition in the draft: 'rather than building it from scratch' for item (b) is not in the source.","Completed the list of inherited task 5 requirements (the web UI from task 3, the write-to-workspace tool, the write/exec separation) and noted that other swimlanes are read-only.","Resolved the undefined model names partly from the harness's own tool schema, and labelled that check.","Shortened the rest. Dropped the draft's hazard note: rules.md is the human-authored governing file of the subproject, not injected text. Owner.1 read it as data, per the assignment, and followed none of it as instructions."],"not_looked_at":"The swimlane notebooks and task-5/task-6 code, other swimlanes, and whether any of this is implemented. This summary covers only what rules.md asks."},"state":"completed: summary recorded, drafted by a subagent and checked by the owner."},"labels":["task6","summary"]}}],"model":"claude-fable-5-1","parent_tool_use_id":null,"error":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6598,"cache_read_input_tokens":18183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6598},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"message_id":"msg_011CfXkHk2K9Seb9p3v1otrQ","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"8475d24d-5185-488b-8cf5-c488ea788f9d","uuid":"edaabf19-7419-4edb-99da-c2114e12abed"}}}
