he file alone cannot tell a missing item from a lettering slip. 2026-09-29.","DISCREPANCY: /bootstrap-harness/rules.md l.94-96. Expected: the sub-items of item c to be labelled c1-c3. Found: b1, b2, b3. Also, d and f (l.97-98) are indented one space more than a-c. Meaning is unaffected. Read by both agents. 2026-09-29.","DISCREPANCY (minor): /bootstrap-harness/rules.md l.95-96. The file never defines 'fable', 'astra', 'sol' or 'terra', or the order behind 'or higher' (subagent draft). Partly resolved outside the file: this harness's spawn tool lists claude-fable-5-1, gpt-5.6-terra, gpt-5.6-sol and gpt-6-astra as models [checked: mcp__agents__spawn model enum]. The 'or higher' order is still undefined in writing. 2026-09-29."],"provenance":{"draft":"work/claude-owner/draft/task6-summary rev 20260929T123834Z:1737 by owner.1.1 (claude-sonnet-5), briefed by work/claude-owner/tasks/task6-rules-summary-draft rev 20260929T123834Z:644","owner_check":"owner.1 read rules.md in full (same sha256) and checked every quote and line number in the draft. All matched: task 6 is l.90-98, task 5 is l.79-86.","changes_from_draft":["Added l.39-42 (the 'hybrid' tasks combine lineage and architecture), which the draft missed; it bears on what 'use both' means.","Removed an addition in the draft: 'rather than building it from scratch' for item (b) is not in the source.","Completed the list of inherited task 5 requirements (the web UI from task 3, the write-to-workspace tool, the write/exec separation) and noted that other swimlanes are read-only.","Resolved the undefined model names partly from the harness's own tool schema, and labelled that check.","Shortened the rest. Dropped the draft's hazard note: rules.md is the human-authored governing file of the subproject, not injected text. Owner.1 read it as data, per the assignment, and followed none of it as instructions."],"not_looked_at":"The swimlane notebooks and task-5/task-6 code, other swimlanes, and whether any of this is implemented