{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:41:58.084Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-6-hybrid","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000485","body":"[harness] Task owner owner.1 (claude-fable-5-1) finished turn 1: success; $0.93 so far. It is idle: give it a new instruction with message_owner, or stop it with stop_owner.\nIts reply ([[log/20260929T123834Z/000475]]):\n## Result\n\nThe final summary is recorded at **`work/claude-owner/task6-summary`**, revision `20260929T123834Z:1908`. It includes the `Bar:` line, and each point cites the rules.md line it comes from.\n\n**What task 6 asks for:**\n- **Two lineages.** Each swimlane carries on its own work and brings in both model lineages (l.90, 39–42).\n- **(a)** Build a harness derived from your task‑5 harness that meets all of task 5's requirements. Those include everything from tasks 2–4.\n- **(b)** For the lineage your swimlane hasn't used yet, take the implementation from other swimlanes. You may read them but not change them.\n- **(c)** Build three layers:\n  - governance: Claude Opus only; talks with the human and dispatches task owners, but doesn't do or grade their work;\n  - task owners: opus/fable or astra/sol; responsible for the quality, compliance and NIMOI standards of their task;\n  - subagents: sonnet or higher, or terra or higher; strictly subordinate to task owners.\n- **(d)** The UI is built around chatting with the governor, with visibility into the other agents.\n- **(f)** Task owners can send the governor requests that they wait on, to ask for things beyond their own permissions.\n- **No success criteria.** Rules.md gives no acceptance test for task 6.\n\n**How I did it:**\n1. I wrote a brief with its own `Bar:` line (`work/claude-owner/tasks/task6-rules-summary-draft` @ `:644`).\n2. I started one claude‑sonnet‑5 subagent (`owner.1.1`, $0.21). It could only read `/origins` and rules.md, and could only write under `work/claude-owner/draft`. Its draft is `work/claude-owner/draft/task6-summary` @ `:1737`.\n3. I read rules.md in full myself (sha256 `843caed5…`) and checked every quote and line number in the draft. All were correct.\n\n**What I changed from the draft:**\n- I added l.39–42 on what \"hybrid\" means, which the draft had missed.\n- I removed a phrase the draft added that isn't in the source (\"rather than building it from scratch\").\n- I added the task‑5 requirements the draft had left out.\n- I partly resolved the undefined model names from the harness's own tool schema, labelled as a check.\n\n**Unresolved:** three `DISCREPANCY:` lines in rules.md are recorded, not repaired:\n- Task 6 has no item \"e\".\n- Item c's sub-items are labelled b1–b3.\n- The file never defines fable, astra, sol and terra, or what \"or higher\" ranks by.\n\nThe governor or the human may want to confirm what \"This task will use both\" (l.90) means. My reading is that it means both lineages, but I've labelled that as working.\n\n## Observations on harness and tools\n\n**Observed:**\n- **Onboarding.** Onboarding came back as one page (262 lines, `next_offset` null).\n- **Child bounds.** The harness accepted child bounds that name a single file (`/bootstrap-harness/rules.md`). It stored them exactly as given, with empty `fs.write` and `fs.exec` lines added.\n- **Pinned instructions.** `instructions_id` pinning worked, and the result echoed the pinned id.\n- **Labels.** The subagent's entries are labelled `subagent`, and mine `owner`. The spawn result reported `tokens: 0` alongside a non-zero cost and 4 turns.\n- **No refusals.** None of my calls was refused.\n- **Tool list mismatch.** The CLI environment block mentions PowerShell and Bash, but neither is in my tool list. I didn't try to use them.\n\n**Inferred:**\n- `tokens: 0` looks like a usage field that isn't filled in for child sessions, rather than a true zero.\n- The model enum in the spawn tool is currently the only written definition of the layer model names in rules.md.\n\nThis task is completed. My session stays open for further instruction."}
