{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:42:02.323Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-6-hybrid","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000501","body":{"kind":"message","agent":"governor","turn":4,"direction":"to_agent","message":{"_type":"UserMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolResultBlock","tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3NLbKjx486L3RwyewWizj","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"ledger\": \"claude-anthropic-harness-t6\",\n \"name\": \"work/claude-owner/task6-summary\",\n \"labels\": [\n  \"agent.owner.1\",\n  \"owner\",\n  \"summary\",\n  \"task6\"\n ],\n \"bound\": true,\n \"deleted\": false,\n \"current\": {\n  \"id\": \"20260929T123834Z:1908\",\n  \"ts\": \"2026-09-29T12:41:40.650Z\",\n  \"author\": \"owner.1@20260929T123834Z:claude-fable-5-1@claude-anthropic-harness\",\n  \"prev\": null,\n  \"body\": {\n   \"title\": \"What task 6 (task-6-hybrid) asks for: plain summary of /bootstrap-harness/rules.md\",\n   \"Bar\": \"A short, plain summary a newcomer could act on. Every statement is traceable to a cited line of rules.md (sha256 843caed5bbad0495430bbd194050e4cff0c99688cdaa80504a052287cfec61c2, 98 lines, read in full by owner.1). Nothing the file says about task 6 is left out, and nothing is added. Inferences are labelled [working], and defects in the source are recorded as DISCREPANCY lines, not smoothed over. Not polished prose, and not an interpretation of how to build it.\",\n   \"summary\": [\n    \"Task 6 continues each swimlane's own line of work, whatever model lineage it started with, and 'will use both' (l.90). Rules.md says of swimlanes that for 'hybrid' tasks the lineage and the initial harness architecture 'will be combined' (l.39-40). [working: 'both' = both lineages, Claude and GPT, and so both architectures, Claude Agent SDK and Codex App Server (l.41-42).]\",\n    \"(a) Build a harness derived from your own task-5 harness that meets all of task 5's requirements (l.91). By task 5a (l.80) those include tasks 2-4: message and tool-call logging, restricted code-execution tools, an 'add' tool, usage/rate-limit logging, the local web UI, per-session ledger logging with protected harness entries, and bounded filesystem read. Task 5 adds a bound notation that is concise and the same for parent and child, a tool that writes a ledger entry's body to a workspace, and a tool that runs Python only from a scripts directory, where agents can never both write and execute. It also adds a harness-owned subagent tool (not the SDK's native one) with subset bounds, required onboarding and ledger-pointer instructions, and Codex exec restricted where possible, with any gaps documented (l.81-86).\",\n    \"(b) For the model lineage your swimlane has not used yet, draw the implementation from other swimlanes (l.92). Cross-pollination is permitted (l.46). Other swimlanes may be read but never modified (l.44-45).\",\n    \"(c) Implement a 3-layer multi-model architecture (l.93). Governance layer (l.94): Claude Opus only. It communicates with the human and dispatches task owners. It must not do task owners' jobs or grade their work beyond what safety or governance needs. Task-owner layer (l.95): Claude opus/fable or GPT astra/sol. It pursues an assigned task, often a written one (a ticket system comes later). It is responsible for the task's quality, for complying with the letter and intent of human and governor instructions and restrictions, and for keeping NIMOI's standards and faithfulness as the t\n...[clipped at 3000 characters; raise max_chars to see more]"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"26e79a95-4cba-494f-8838-57a3817e73b9","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"ledger\": \"claude-anthropic-harness-t6\",\n \"name\": \"work/claude-owner/task6-summary\",\n \"labels\": [\n  \"agent.owner.1\",\n  \"owner\",\n  \"summary\",\n  \"task6\"\n ],\n \"bound\": true,\n \"deleted\": false,\n \"current\": {\n  \"id\": \"20260929T123834Z:1908\",\n  \"ts\": \"2026-09-29T12:41:40.650Z\",\n  \"author\": \"owner.1@20260929T123834Z:claude-fable-5-1@claude-anthropic-harness\",\n  \"prev\": null,\n  \"body\": {\n   \"title\": \"What task 6 (task-6-hybrid) asks for: plain summary of /bootstrap-harness/rules.md\",\n   \"Bar\": \"A short, plain summary a newcomer could act on. Every statement is traceable to a cited line of rules.md (sha256 843caed5bbad0495430bbd194050e4cff0c99688cdaa80504a052287cfec61c2, 98 lines, read in full by owner.1). Nothing the file says about task 6 is left out, and nothing is added. Inferences are labelled [working], and defects in the source are recorded as DISCREPANCY lines, not smoothed over. Not polished prose, and not an interpretation of how to build it.\",\n   \"summary\": [\n    \"Task 6 continues each swimlane's own line of work, whatever model lineage it started with, and 'will use both' (l.90). Rules.md says of swimlanes that for 'hybrid' tasks the lineage and the initial harness architecture 'will be combined' (l.39-40). [working: 'both' = both lineages, Claude and GPT, and so both architectures, Claude Agent SDK and Codex App Server (l.41-42).]\",\n    \"(a) Build a harness derived from your own task-5 harness that meets all of task 5's requirements (l.91). By task 5a (l.80) those include tasks 2-4: message and tool-call logging, restricted code-execution tools, an 'add' tool, usage/rate-limit logging, the local web UI, per-session ledger logging with protected harness entries, and bounded filesystem read. Task 5 adds a bound notation that is concise and the same for parent and child, a tool that writes a ledger entry's body to a workspace, and a tool that runs Python only from a scripts directory, where agents can never both write and execute. It also adds a harness-owned subagent tool (not the SDK's native one) with subset bounds, required onboarding and ledger-pointer instructions, and Codex exec restricted where possible, with any gaps documented (l.81-86).\",\n    \"(b) For the model lineage your swimlane has not used yet, draw the implementation from other swimlanes (l.92). Cross-pollination is permitted (l.46). Other swimlanes may be read but never modified (l.44-45).\",\n    \"(c) Implement a 3-layer multi-model architecture (l.93). Governance layer (l.94): Claude Opus only. It communicates with the human and dispatches task owners. It must not do task owners' jobs or grade their work beyond what safety or governance needs. Task-owner layer (l.95): Claude opus/fable or GPT astra/sol. It pursues an assigned task, often a written one (a ticket system comes later). It is responsible for the task's quality, for complying with the letter and intent of human and governor instructions and restrictions, and for keeping NIMOI's standards and faithfulness as the t\n...[clipped at 3000 characters; raise max_chars to see more]"}],"origin":null}}}
