{"ts":"2026-09-29T12:42:29.922Z","author":"governor@20260929T123834Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T123834Z/000551","body":"Both owners have reported and I've stopped both; the run is complete. Neither owner was refused or needed anything from me: no requests, no extra permissions, no more budget. My run note is at `gov/runs/20260929-two-owner-test`.\n\n**What each produced:**\n- **Claude owner** (owner.1, claude-fable-5-1). It delegated the reading and first draft to one claude-sonnet-5 subagent, restricted to reading `/origins` and `rules.md` and writing drafts under `work/claude-owner/draft`. Then it read `rules.md` in full itself and checked the draft line by line. It fixed an omission, removed a phrase the draft had invented, and recorded a summary with line citations at `work/claude-owner/task6-summary` (cost about $0.93). It also flagged three problems in `rules.md` without changing anything:\n  - task 6 has no item \"e\";\n  - item c's sub-items are labelled b1–b3;\n  - the model names fable, astra, sol and terra are never defined, nor what \"or higher\" means.\n- **GPT owner** (owner.2, gpt-5.6-sol). The same pattern with one gpt-5.6-terra subagent, which the log confirms. It produced a shorter plain summary at `work/gpt-owner/task6-summary` that cites the task-5 and task-6 line ranges (about 74k tokens). Its reading of task 6 matches the Claude owner's. I haven't checked either summary against `rules.md` myself.\n\n**Notable harness behaviour:**\n- **Possible budget bug.** The GPT owner's subagent was started with a dollar limit equal to the whole remaining launch budget ($4.79). The Claude owner's subagent got $1.50. The difference traces to the GPT owner having no allowance of its own. I checked this in the log entries (`000167` and `000175`), and I think it needs fixing.\n- **`Bar:` lines.** Both owners wrote `Bar:` lines into their own results because onboarding 1.12 says they must, and the harness accepted them; its refusal only covers assignments and messages. I had put \"the bar is yours to set\" in the assignments, and neither owner stopped to ask for one. The mismatch between onboarding and the founder's 2026-09-29 rule is still there for the founder to settle.\n- **Minor items the Claude owner reported:**\n  - its subagent's result showed `tokens: 0` alongside a non-zero cost;\n  - the CLI text names Bash and PowerShell, but neither is in its tool list;\n  - `rules.md` never defines the model names except through the spawn tool's own model list.\n- **The record.** Both subagents' sessions and bounds are in the harness log as expected. My search for a \"refusal\" label found nothing, but I'm not certain that's the name the harness uses. So \"no refusals\" is based on the owners' reports."}
